      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "663988e007e47e87a3251ece",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Setup:\n\n - A group owner has set the group joining mechanism \"Open to New Members\" to \"Request Invite\"\n\n- A user who already joined the maximum allowed number of groups wants to join that group\n\nCurrent behavior:\n\nThe group owner gets a notification about the join request but can't resolve it or message the user back. His only options are: ignore or decline the request.\n\nInstead what should happen:\n\nWhen a user has already joined the maximum allowed number of groups he should not be able to request to join a group. Instead he should receive an error message: \"You can not join any more groups as you have already joined the maximum allowed number of groups.\"",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Groups: Request Invite behavior (when user joined max number of groups)",
